The '''Mirror-Spires''' of [[Ivexia]]<ref name="TROS VD" /> were a series of shining [[Color|white]] towers with numerous reflective surfaces.<ref name="TROSEE">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: Expanded Edition]]''</ref> While trying to escape [[First Order]] [[First Order military|forces]]<ref name="TROS VD" /> in [[35 ABY]],<ref name="Date">{{FilmDate|IX|the appearance of the Mirror-Spires}}</ref> [[Resistance pilot]] [[Poe Dameron]] [[Hyperspace skipping|jumped]] from the [[Crystal Chaos]] of [[Cardovyte]] to the spires,<ref name="TROS VD" /> with several [[TIE/wi Interceptor]]s in pursuit.<ref name="TROSEE" />

A readout on the ''Falcon'' identified the spires and the reflective surfaces made it difficult for [[Finn]], a [[Resistance]] member aboard the ''Falcon'', to tell how many [[starfighter]]s were pursuing them and which towers were real and which only reflections. Dameron barely avoided a collision as several of the [[TIE series|TIEs]] crashed, before jumping the ''Falcon'' again to the [[Typhonic Nebula]].<ref name="TROSEE" />

{{Loc-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|From the 90s Illustrated Star Wars Universe book; inspired "Mirrorworld" in the TROS lightspeed skipping bit.|Pablo Hidalgo|<ref name="Pablo">{{Twitter|pabl0hidalgo|status/1563404046609747973|[[Pablo Hidalgo]]|quote=From the 90s Illustrated Star Wars Universe book; inspired "Mirrorworld" in the TROS lightspeed skipping bit.|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/PsoKC}}</ref>}}
The Mirror-Spires first appeared in the [[2019]] [[sequel trilogy]] film, [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']],<ref name="TROS">{{Film|IX}}</ref> and was first identified in the accompanying reference book ''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]'', which was written by [[Pablo Hidalgo]].<ref name="TROS VD" /> It was inspired by [[Ralph McQuarrie]] artwork from ''[[The Illustrated Star Wars Universe]]''.<ref name="Pablo" />

